<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Meenakshi of Madurai</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1736</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Meenakshi was the last ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madurai-nayak-dynasty">Madurai Nayak dynasty</a>, governing as queen from the early 1730s after the death of her husband <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vijaya-ranga-chokkanatha">Vijaya Ranga Chokkanatha</a>. Disputes over the succession drew in the Nawab of the Carnatic, whose officer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chanda-sahib">Chanda Sahib</a> seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiruchirappalli">Tiruchirappalli</a> and imprisoned her in 1736. She is said to have taken poison, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nayaka">Nayak</a> kingdom passed to the Carnatic nawabs.</p></div>
